      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.93,
      "end_seconds": 225.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.42,
      "end_seconds": 244.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this is probably an enlarged prostate causing urinary symptoms. Let's book kidney function tests to look into urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.21,
      "end_seconds": 246.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.64,
      "end_seconds": 253.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "We should do an ultrasound of the bladder and prostate for urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.65,
      "end_seconds": 255.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "mm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.51,
      "end_seconds": 264.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "We'll begin with tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night, for four weeks. That should help with urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.77,
      "end_seconds": 269.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "How long until it works?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.89,
      "end_seconds": 297.39,
      "duration_seconds": 26.5,
      "text": "cut back on tea and coffee after the afternoon and go before you sleep don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day the urology clinic would be the right next step, I'll refer you keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.24,
      "end_seconds": 300.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Okay, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.27,
      "end_seconds": 304.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "let's review you in four weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
